            <ArticleTitle>A double blind single dose comparison between two analgesics, rimazolium and acetylsalicylic acid in oral surgery outpatients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The relief of pain after extraction of a mandibular third molar by two analgesics, rimazolium and acetylsalicylic acid (ASA) was studied in three groups of patients, who received either of these analgesics or a placebo. A questionnaire and careful instructions on its use were given to the patients. ASA had a better effect than both rimazolium and placebo. The results are discussed with regard to differences between analgesics with or without anti-inflammatory properties.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
